# JavaScript Rules

## XSS Prevention
- Use `.textContent` or jQuery `.text()` for untrusted data, NEVER `.innerHTML` or `.html()`
- Use jQuery `.css()` for dynamic styling instead of string-concatenated style attributes

## Defensive Checks
- Guard globals: `typeof fxw_checkout_params !== 'undefined'` before access
- Guard response data: `response.success && response.data` before accessing `.message`
- Validate DOM selectors: regex-check dynamic IDs before `$('#' + id)`
- Use `document.getElementById(id)` instead of `$('#' + userInput)` to prevent selector injection

## AJAX Patterns
- Always include nonce in AJAX data
- Handle both `.success` and `.fail`/`error` callbacks
- Provide user-friendly fallback messages
